      "content": "You should generally categorize the chair as a business expense, but only if you can demonstrate a clear connection between the item and your business activities, rather than treating it as a personal draw for comfort. Since it's located in your home, you'll likely need to allocate a percentage of the business use (e.g., time used in the dedicated studio) or report depreciation costs rather than writing off the entire purchase. Always attach specific business records, like dates of use in a private studio versus the bedroom, to substantiate this as a legitimate expense to the IRS or tax authorities. If the chair is primarily for personal relaxation within the same space, tax laws may consider it a mixed-use asset requiring careful allocation.",
