      "content": "For mixed-use items like software or office supplies, you must split the cost based on actual business usage: track how many hours are spent on work versus personal tasks to allocate the expense correctly. Many subscriptions, like cloud accounting tools, are fully deductible if purchased specifically for business management, so check if the specific app allows you to separate work and personal accounts. Maintaining a simple log noting the date, purpose of use, and context for research or purchases will help you differentiate legitimate deductibles from personal drawings in future tax returns. This documentation is crucial because the IRS requires clear evidence that the expense was incurred for business purposes, not just for convenience.",
